From fc80a190a17c9ad67d521796818b6102d3512d0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicola Nicodemo <nicola084@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:36:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-14:
 enable the fingerprint reader

The 14" (NP940XMA) has an EgisTec match-on-chip fingerprint sensor
(USB 1c7a:05a1, ETU905A80-E, libfprint egismoc) on the usb_2 controller
(usb@a200000): Windows shows it on port 0 of \_SB.USB4 (QCOM0D09,
registers at 0xa200000), whose _CRS also takes TLMM 184, the reset of the
PTN3222 eUSB2 repeater already described as eusb6_repeater in
x1e-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge.dtsi.

Enable usb_2 in host mode and its high-speed PHY behind that repeater, with
the supplies other X1E boards give usb_2_hsphy. The sensor enumerates and
fprintd drives it (enrolment runs to completion). Keeping prints on the
sensor needs SDCP in libfprint (MR !547, not merged); that is userspace.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VZvhNtszdDfmc8XTwbYbqN
Signed-off-by: Nicola Nicodemo <nicola084@gmail.com>
---
 .../x1e80100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-14.dts    | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-14.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-14.dts
index 47c2b8f7e..b599720ca 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-14.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-14.dts
@@ -200,3 +200,19 @@ left_tweeter: speaker@0,1 {
 		qcom,port-mapping = <4 5 6 7>;
 	};
 };
+
+/* Fingerprint reader (EgisTec 1c7a:05a1) on usb_2. */
+&usb_2 {
+	dr_mode = "host";
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&usb_2_hsphy {
+	vdd-supply = <&vreg_l2e_0p8>;
+	vdda12-supply = <&vreg_l3e_1p2>;
+
+	phys = <&eusb6_repeater>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
-- 
